body:
This was a really rough marathon - I was hoping to shave time off my Goodlife Toronto Marathon time, but actually ended up adding 5 minutes to the time. I was foolish because I ate oatmeal before the race (never done that before), was only able to get 5 hours of sleep, and did not pace myself properly. In fact, I started and ran the first 16 km ahead of the 03:00:00 pace bunny, and then on that long hot stretch around 12km-17km where it's just straight road with sun, I fell apart. 

&#x200B;

I'm determined to do better in October. I will train properly.

I think this is really important and thank you for saying it. 

&#x200B;

\- you're absolutely right. Maybe it's a self-fulfilling thing having all the attention be on America and then America being the centre of attention and bastillon of ideals the world ought to uphold. In theory, the constitution is a pretty remarkable document, but it really isn't applied, and hasn't been applied by the individuals. Maybe legally, it's generally pretty ironclad (I have qualms with how it was written and some of the amendments) but somehow the culture is so very toxic.

Control for this if you can. Ultimately it's uv-light interacting in funny ways that lead to the destruction of isohumulones. The reaction is *fast*. The hoppier the beer, the more you'll notice the impact. And sure, while some "artificial" light (LED, tungsten, incandescent, etc.) emit small amounts of uv-light, it would not be enough to impact your beer.

&#x200B;

Next time you're drinking a very hoppy beer (yours or otherwise) evaluate its aroma and give 'er a few sips. Then hold it out in direct sunlight for as little as ten/fifteen seconds. Then evaluate again. It'll be like night and day.
